# Docker build context hygiene (CIS Docker Benchmark 4.4 / image build files).
#
# Without this file the whole repository is sent to the Docker daemon on every
# build — including .git history and a local .env, which .gitignore does NOT
# protect, because the ignore rules that matter here are the context ones.
#
# target/ is deliberately NOT ignored: the Dockerfile copies
# target/pad-liveness-backend-*-slim.jar out of it.
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
*.iml
*.log

# Local secrets and machine overrides — never needed to build the image.
# Same rule as .gitignore: the .env file docker compose reads automatically,
# and the ./secrets/ directory docs/configuration.md mounts from.
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks

# Build output that is not the jar the image copies.
# android_client/build alone is ~690 MB.
android_client/build
android_client/android/.gradle
android_client/.dart_tool
**/node_modules

# Python build/runtime caches.
pad_liveness_backend/.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
